IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `imm-types`

-- Immigration Act 2009 — GOAL 4: EMPLOYERS.
--
--   "Does the employer commit an offence by allowing this person to work?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2009_51.txt — s 350.

§ `Goal 4 — employers`

-- s 350 "(1) Every employer commits an offence ... who allows, or continues
-- to allow, any person to work in that employer's service, knowing that the
-- person is not entitled under this Act to do that work. ... (3) ... an
-- employer is treated as knowing that an employee is not entitled ... if, at
-- any time in the preceding 12 months ..., the employer has been informed of
-- that fact in writing by an immigration officer. (4) No employer is liable
-- ... in respect of any period during which the employer continues to allow
-- any person to work ... in compliance with the minimum requirements of any
-- employment agreement ... relating to the giving of notice on termination".
-- "The preceding 12 months" counts back from the day of work, its
-- anniversary included (fork F1).
@ref s 350(1), (3)-(4)
@export Whether an employer commits an offence under s 350 of the Immigration Act 2009 (NZ) by allowing a person to work on a day: the person is not entitled to do the work, the employer knew it (or was told so in writing by an immigration officer in the preceding 12 months), and the employer is not merely working out the employment agreement's minimum notice period. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`  @desc The day of work, the person's entitlement, the employer's knowledge or written notice, and any notice period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer commits an offence under s 350` e IF
        NOT e's `the person is entitled to do the work`
    AND (   e's `the employer knew the person was not entitled`
         OR (CONSIDER e's `informed in writing by an immigration officer on`
             WHEN JUST told THEN told AT MOST work AND told AT LEAST `add years` work (0 MINUS 1)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))
    AND NOT e's `within the employment agreement's minimum notice period`
    WHERE
        work MEANS e's `allowed the person to work on`
